        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add session thread management",
        "body": "Related: #54397\nCloses #88568\n\nAI-assisted: yes. The implementation was reviewed with the repository's structured autoreview workflow.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw sessions are durable conversation threads, but their management controls are fragmented. Frequent sessions disappear into recency ordering, stale sessions remain in every active list unless deleted, and renaming is disconnected from the primary Chat session picker.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds pin, archive/restore, and rename controls to the existing session model instead of introducing a second topic store or fork system. `sessions.list` now separates active and archived sessions, `sessions.patch` owns management mutations, live `sessions.changed` events keep every subscribed UI coherent, and the existing session fork/branch paths remain canonical.\n\nThe behavior uses first-class rename, archive, and restore contracts while preserving OpenClaw's gateway/session ownership boundaries.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can now:\n\n- rename, pin/unpin, and archive sessions directly from the Chat session picker;\n- keep pinned active sessions above newer unpinned sessions;\n- switch the Sessions page into an archived-only view and restore sessions without losing transcripts;\n- inspect archived sessions through `sessions_list`.\n\nAgent main sessions and sessions with active runs cannot be archived. Archiving clears the pin, and archiving the selected Chat session returns the UI to that agent's main session.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm test src/gateway/sessions-patch.test.ts src/gateway/session-utils.test.ts src/gateway/server.sessions.store-rpc.test.ts src/gateway/server.sessions.delete-lifecycle.test.ts src/gateway/server.sessions.list-changed.test.ts src/agents/tools/sessions-list-tool.test.ts ui/src/ui/controllers/sessions.test.ts ui/src/ui/views/sessions.test.ts ui/src/ui/views/chat.test.ts ui/src/ui/app-render.helpers.node.test.ts` — 1,060 tests passed across four shards.\n- `OPENCLAW_CAPTURE_UI_PROOF=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.ui-e2e.config.ts --configLoader runner ui/src/ui/e2e/session-management.e2e.test.ts` — real Chromium GUI flow passed for rename, pin/unpin, archive, and protected main-session behavior.\n\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"900\" alt=\"Chat session picker with rename, pin, and archive controls\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bc88d276-73a5-4e69-b561-7411b496c031\" />\n\n- `pnpm tsgo:core` — passed.\n- `pnpm tsgo:test:ui` — passed.\n- `pnpm build` — passed, including Control UI production build.\n- `pnpm protocol:check` — passed after commit; Swift protocol regeneration is stable and new optional initializer arguments preserve source compatibility.\n- Structured autoreview — clean after resolving Swift initializer compatibility and multi-client `sessions.changed` coherence findings.\n- `pnpm check:changed` reached the core-test type lane remotely on AWS Crabbox (`run_e424f6067046`) and stopped on four untouched current-main errors in `server-cron-notifications.test.ts`, `server-cron.test.ts`, and `llm/providers/anthropic.test.ts`; every preceding changed check and core typecheck passed.\n",
